diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Layer-2 VLAN configuration on the office access switch (switch1). Mechanism: The two desks are no longer in the same broadcast domain, so Windows/SMB discovery (NetBIOS/mDNS/broadcasts) and “seeing each other” fails, even though routed IP connectivity may still allow manual pings.

Localization: On switch1, ports for the nearby laptops are split across two VLAN bridges:
- br_vlan10 members include eth3 and eth4 (where laptop2 172.16.10.12 and laptop3 172.16.10.13 connect).
- br_vlan20 contains eth7 (where laptop0 172.16.20.10 connects).

Evidence:
- laptop2 ↔ laptop3 ping succeeds (same subnet 172.16.10.0/24).
- laptop2/3 ↔ laptop0 ping also succeeds but with TTL 63, indicating inter-VLAN routing
